The National Robotics Competition database is a relational PostgreSQL database designed to manage information about participants, schools, teams, robots, competitions, rounds, judges, scores, and awards.

The database applies relational database design principles, primary and foreign keys, integrity constraints, normalization, SQL queries, analytical functions, views, and reporting.

The completed project demonstrates the full database development process from requirements analysis and ER modeling to implementation, data manipulation, analysis, reporting, and final documentation.
